   $q$In paragraph 4, the meaning of each signal is kept "arcane." This most nearly means:$q$, $q$[{"text":"understood by only a few people","is_correct":true},{"text":"extremely old and outdated","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"surface-association"},{"text":"obvious to anyone watching","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"written down in careful detail","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$understood by only a few people$q$, $q$The meaning was "known only to a small group of trained clerks," and an observer "could see every movement and still have no idea," so arcane means understood by only a few. Being obvious to observers is the opposite of the situation the paragraph describes.$q$, 'draft', 'e2689ef4-27fd-53dc-9fbe-469045b5c079')
