   $q$The author follows "Ostensibly" with a contrast. What does "ostensibly" mean in paragraph 2?$q$, $q$[{"text":"as it was done long ago","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unrelated-meaning"},{"text":"as it truly turned out","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"as it appeared on the surface","is_correct":true},{"text":"as it was written in the rules","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$as it appeared on the surface$q$, $q$The job seemed simple, but "In practice, it was nothing of the kind," so ostensibly means as it appeared on the surface. "As it truly turned out" describes the "In practice" sentence, which is the contrast, not the meaning.$q$, 'draft', '05050e51-5404-579d-af75-41336f95f769')
