   $q$Which detail from the passage best supports the idea that heavy traffic is linked with fewer lichen species?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Trees along the busy ring road averaged three species, while park trees far from roads averaged eleven.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Nandakumar plans to repeat the survey in five years to study a new zone.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"The team chose trees of the same species and similar age for the survey.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"A single trained volunteer can survey dozens of trees in a day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-different-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Trees along the busy ring road averaged three species, while park trees far from roads averaged eleven.$q$, $q$The comparison of three species on the busiest road with eleven in parks far from roads directly connects traffic with fewer species. The detail about volunteers supports the claim that lichen surveys are cheap, not the link to traffic.$q$, 'draft', '23cfc83d-ad00-5c09-844e-bd91e4f2b73b')
