  ('cdbdd073-29c4-53a0-aa36-798c90844d14', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-evidence-inference'), null, 'medium',
   $q$What can most reasonably be inferred about the delicate, leafy lichens described in the second paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They are the only lichens that can serve as accurate monitors of nitrogen dioxide.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"They need more sunlight than the yellow type, which is why they grow in open parks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They are probably less able to tolerate polluted air than the yellow lichens found near the ring road.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They were removed from ring road trees by the street sweepers that clean the city.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They are probably less able to tolerate polluted air than the yellow lichens found near the ring road.$q$, $q$The leafy forms appeared in parks but were "absent near the ring road," where the surviving lichens were "a tolerant yellow type," so the leafy forms are likely less tolerant. The text never compares the sunlight needs of the two types, so that choice adds an unsupported cause.$q$, 'draft', '23cfc83d-ad00-5c09-844e-bd91e4f2b73b')
