  ('7a86cd8a-bdff-5a77-8fa0-ee776c511a01', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-evidence-inference'), null, 'hard',
   $q$A city official argues that lichen surveys could fully replace Callowmere's electronic air stations. Which detail from the passage most weakens this argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A tree's lichen community reflects years of conditions rather than last week's air.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Trees near stations with higher nitrogen dioxide levels tended to carry fewer species.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-opposing-claim"},{"text":"Each electronic station costs more than the city's yearly budget for tree care.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-opposing-claim"},{"text":"Lichens are partnerships between a fungus and an organism that uses sunlight.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A tree's lichen community reflects years of conditions rather than last week's air.$q$, $q$If lichens show only long-term conditions, they cannot report short-term changes in air quality the way stations can, which undercuts full replacement. The cost detail actually favors the official's argument, so it does not weaken it.$q$, 'draft', '23cfc83d-ad00-5c09-844e-bd91e4f2b73b')
