   $q$According to the passage, how did Brenford's storage houses keep ice from melting quickly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They stored only ice that was at least twelve inches thick.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-detail"},{"text":"They had double walls packed with sawdust that slowed melting.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They used conveyors to keep the blocks moving and exposed to wind.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-detail"},{"text":"They were built partly underground along the cold shore of the lake.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They had double walls packed with sawdust that slowed melting.$q$, $q$The second paragraph says the houses "had double walls packed with sawdust, which slowed melting." The twelve-inch figure describes when harvesting began, not how the ice was stored.$q$, 'draft', '8800749b-2ae2-5f2d-8c44-13606e370353')
