   $q$Which detail best supports the claim that ice harvesting was attractive work for local farmers?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Brenford's ice traveled by rail to cities as far as three hundred miles away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-different-claim"},{"text":"The work paid better than most winter jobs, and farmers had little to do between harvests.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Managers considered losing a third of the harvest to melting acceptable.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Workers used horse-drawn plows with steel teeth to score the ice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The work paid better than most winter jobs, and farmers had little to do between harvests.$q$, $q$Better pay during a season when farmers "had little to do" explains why they "often joined the crews." The rail detail shows how far the ice was sold, not why farmers wanted the work.$q$, 'draft', '8800749b-2ae2-5f2d-8c44-13606e370353')
