  ('3d7ab1fa-3197-521e-bec1-ce4bd2313d5e', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-evidence-inference'), null, 'medium',
   $q$What can most reasonably be inferred from the detail that attendance among older boys dropped sharply every January?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Brenford's schools closed each January because the roads were covered in ice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Older boys in Brenford were less interested in school than younger students were.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Many older boys likely left school during the harvest season to work on the ice crews.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The ice companies required families to send their sons to work each winter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Many older boys likely left school during the harvest season to work on the ice crews.$q$, $q$The drop happens in January, when the passage says harvesting took place, and it comes right after the sentence about farmers joining the crews, so work on the ice is the best explanation. Nothing in the text mentions school closings or a company requirement.$q$, 'draft', '8800749b-2ae2-5f2d-8c44-13606e370353')
