   $q$According to the passage, why did the library need character recognition software after scanning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The scanned images were too dark for most readers to see clearly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The library had to translate the oldest papers into modern spelling.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A photograph of a page is only an image, so its words cannot be searched.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The software repaired the brittle pages so they could be scanned again.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A photograph of a page is only an image, so its words cannot be searched.$q$, $q$The second paragraph explains that "a photograph of a page is just an image," so a search will not find words inside it, and the software was used "to make the text searchable." Brittle pages were handled with a cradle, not with software.$q$, 'draft', '914ee808-4690-58a9-b0a8-2131e39903e0')
