   $q$According to the passage, what happened to timer violations during the 2022 season?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They were counted only for batters, not for pitchers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They stayed at about three per game for the entire season.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"They rose steadily as pitchers grew more tired late in the season.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"They fell from almost three per game to fewer than one by midseason.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They fell from almost three per game to fewer than one by midseason.$q$, $q$The second paragraph says violations averaged "almost three per game" in the first two weeks and dropped to "fewer than one per game by midseason." The tired arms that pitchers reported were not connected to violations.$q$, 'draft', '7e56376e-1bed-526d-829c-a1b8af742f4b')
