  ('008fd917-02de-5f31-ae17-2abf7ff4476f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-evidence-inference'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which evidence did the researchers use to conclude that the tags were unlikely to change the gliders' behavior much?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Tagged gliders traveled as far as 130 kilometers in a single day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-different-claim"},{"text":"Tagged and untagged gliders in an enclosure flew and rested in similar ways.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The tags weighed about three hundred milligrams and were glued underneath.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Thousands of untagged gliders were counted flying south at Sorrel Point.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Tagged and untagged gliders in an enclosure flew and rested in similar ways.$q$, $q$The team compared forty tagged and forty untagged gliders and found "nearly identical speeds" and similar resting time, then drew its conclusion "so" from that comparison. The tag's weight describes the device but is not the test the conclusion rests on.$q$, 'draft', '2e1a92dc-63ae-5d19-8a5f-48f18cf020e7')
