   $q$According to the passage, why could Varga not use the long sight lines that surveyors normally relied on?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The mud was too deep for her to set up her instruments.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-detail"},{"text":"The land office would not pay for the proper equipment.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Tall reeds in the marsh blocked her view across the land.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Fog over the river mouth hid distant landmarks each day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Tall reeds in the marsh blocked her view across the land.$q$, $q$The second paragraph states, "Because tall reeds blocked her view, she could not use the long sight lines." Deep mud is mentioned only as something her depth pole sometimes could not measure.$q$, 'draft', 'c765a03d-0010-5fed-bd58-8ae1acfa8c8d')
