   $q$What can most reasonably be inferred about why the 1874 survey showed only nineteen channels?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Many channels had filled with mud between 1871 and 1874 and no longer existed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-evidence"},{"text":"Its team, working only nine days in the marsh, probably missed many channels.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Its team counted only the channels deep enough for a boat to pass through.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Varga had invented extra channels to make her survey seem more thorough.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Its team, working only nine days in the marsh, probably missed many channels.$q$, $q$The passage contrasts Varga's eleven weeks with the other team's nine days, and the 1952 photographs showed the channels Varga recorded, so the shorter survey most likely missed them. If channels had filled in by 1874, the 1952 photographs would not still match Varga's map.$q$, 'draft', 'c765a03d-0010-5fed-bd58-8ae1acfa8c8d')
