  ('6201324c-1d1d-5c14-b620-c050c4d99b37', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-figurative-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Mateo says, "The hardest note in the program is the one that is supposed to be the easiest." What does this paradox mean in context?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Easy music is boring, so musicians tend to play it carelessly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A simple note becomes hard because everyone hears it played alone.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The printed concert program listed the notes in the wrong order.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The A is a very high note that is tricky for an oboe to reach.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A simple note becomes hard because everyone hears it played alone.$q$, $q$Mateo explains his own paradox: "Everyone hears it, and nobody is playing anything else to cover it," so the pressure, not the technique, makes it hard. Nothing in the passage says the note is technically difficult to play.$q$, 'draft', 'b5771e20-4539-5867-a8a1-125a9250a969')
