values
  ('7958bddb-ca65-5a21-a5b2-bb67ae949f95', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Mateo tells Nadia, "You were alone up there with sixty people." How does the final paragraph resolve this paradox?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that the other musicians ignored her, so she felt lonely onstage.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It reveals that Mateo was criticizing her for not watching the others.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"It explains that she played the note by herself, but its purpose was to unite everyone.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It explains that only sixty people came to the concert that evening.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It explains that she played the note by herself, but its purpose was to unite everyone.$q$, $q$The last line says the note "belonged to her alone, but it only mattered because everyone else was waiting to join it," so she was both alone and part of the group. Mateo is encouraging her, not describing real loneliness, as her laughter shows.$q$, 'draft', 'b5771e20-4539-5867-a8a1-125a9250a969')
