   $q$The author says a parking lot "can feel like the inside of an oven." What is the purpose of this exaggeration?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To explain that parking lots are used to bake or cook food","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"To argue that parking lots should be closed during summer","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To show that parking lots cool down faster than city parks","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"To help readers feel how intensely hot the pavement becomes","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To help readers feel how intensely hot the pavement becomes$q$, $q$The oven comparison makes the heat vivid and sets up the contrast with the cooler park nearby. The author never argues for closing lots, and the passage says paved areas stay hot, not that they cool faster.$q$, 'draft', 'cdce2745-3cc2-59f5-9849-e7b32611a803')
