values
  ('25266a1a-9ee0-5147-9509-b739e75bec5d', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-figurative-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Planners say cooling a city "is a matter of small choices repeated thousands of times." What idea does this phrase emphasize?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Real change comes from many modest actions that add up together.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Planners must vote on the same decision thousands of times.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Small neighborhoods matter more than large ones in the city.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"},{"text":"One dramatic invention will eventually solve the problem alone.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Real change comes from many modest actions that add up together.$q$, $q$The next sentence explains that one white roof does little, but "thousands of reflective roofs" combined with trees and pavement make "a measurable difference." The phrase rejects the idea of a single dramatic fix.$q$, 'draft', 'cdce2745-3cc2-59f5-9849-e7b32611a803')
