values
  ('019ec1cb-c145-572a-979e-679ed5def922', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-figurative-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The author states that "the most effective cooling tools are often the least dramatic." What makes this statement a paradox?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It means that trees work only in neighborhoods that already are cool.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It claims that cooling tools are both cheap and expensive at once.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"},{"text":"It suggests that dramatic technology is the only way to cool a city.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It says the plainest solutions, like trees, may work better than flashy ones.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It says the plainest solutions, like trees, may work better than flashy ones.$q$, $q$It seems contradictory that something unimpressive would be most powerful, yet the author explains that "a row of maples" may outperform "an expensive new machine." The statement favors plain tools, so it does not call technology the only option.$q$, 'draft', 'cdce2745-3cc2-59f5-9849-e7b32611a803')
