   $q$Freshmen hear that the hill "was a mountain" that "went straight up into the clouds." What is the effect of this exaggeration?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that the hill's reputation had grown bigger than the hill.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that the hill is the tallest point in the whole state.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It reveals that the coach made up stories to scare new runners.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It explains why the team avoids running the hill at practice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows that the hill's reputation had grown bigger than the hill.$q$, $q$Priya is "almost disappointed" when she sees that the hill ends "at a fence and a water tower, not at the edge of the sky," so the stories inflated it. The passage never says who started the stories, so blaming the coach is unsupported.$q$, 'draft', '58f2c27b-5111-5491-9882-ceb303dad66f')
