  ('d0c2aa29-36ef-56b8-b60c-6f664f49c921', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-figurative-language'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Historians call the blank spaces "the most honest parts of an old map." What does this description mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Blank spaces were where explorers later found real islands.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Mapmakers left areas blank to save time and money on printing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The blank areas were drawn with the most careful, accurate lines.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"},{"text":"Empty areas truthfully admit that the mapmaker did not know.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Empty areas truthfully admit that the mapmaker did not know.$q$, $q$The next sentence explains that "an empty area admits plainly that the mapmaker does not know," which is why it is honest. Blank spaces have no lines at all, so the "careful lines" choice misreads what is being praised.$q$, 'draft', '785f8d37-79b3-5bda-9bc0-56a4f5a84eee')
