values
  ('5598618e-93cf-5a7b-b2d0-ac4f60ba81bc', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-figurative-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The author claims that "the emptiness carries information of its own." Why does this statement seem contradictory, and what does it actually mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Empty spaces hide secret symbols, so they only seem to be blank.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Empty spaces show where the ocean is deepest, so they hold depth data.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"},{"text":"Nothing seems to say nothing, yet a blank marks where reliable knowledge ends.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Empty spaces show the mapmaker's mistakes, so they warn readers away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-opposite"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Nothing seems to say nothing, yet a blank marks where reliable knowledge ends.$q$, $q$It sounds impossible for emptiness to inform, but the author explains that it "tells the reader exactly where the trustworthy part of the map ends." The blanks avoid mistakes rather than showing them, since mistakes appear in drawn coastlines.$q$, 'draft', '785f8d37-79b3-5bda-9bc0-56a4f5a84eee')
