values
  ('3025131d-9014-54a4-9215-2fe190507452', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Marisol says, "You spend all day counting what you already have, and somehow you end up with more than you started with." Based on the final paragraph, what does she mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Counting mistakes made the shop's totals higher than before.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Besides the bulbs, Luis gained a real knowledge of the shop.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She means only that Luis found a forgotten box of new bulbs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"The shop will earn more money after the inventory is done.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Besides the bulbs, Luis gained a real knowledge of the shop.$q$, $q$The narrator says Luis "realized she did not only mean the bulbs" and that "he knew the shop now," so the "more" she means includes his understanding of the shop. The bulbs are part of the meaning, but stopping there is too narrow.$q$, 'draft', 'ec8d744b-1d31-56d1-934a-eec6d0c0236b')
