-- Passage rg11-literary-structure-pov-p01
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('f3dc3dc6-dbf4-557d-9b30-44a4cc4d1e85', 'rg11-literary-structure-pov-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '9-12', $q$A Message from the Picnic Committee$q$, $q$The Maple Hollow Neighborhood Association is proud to announce that, after fourteen months of careful planning, this year's community picnic has been made completely safe.

Last year's picnic, as residents will remember, was a near disaster. A flying disk landed in the potato salad. Two children laughed so loudly that a retired piano tuner on Elm Court had to close his window. Several guests reported enjoying themselves without first completing the Enjoyment Registration Form, a lapse the committee does not intend to repeat.

This year, the committee has introduced several improvements. All flying disks have been replaced with a single foam ball, which may be tossed only by a certified Ball Supervisor and only in a straight line. Laughter will be permitted between 2:15 and 2:25 in the designated Laughter Zone, located behind the recycling bins for acoustic reasons. Food will be served in sealed containers, and residents are asked not to open them, since opened containers create crumbs, and crumbs create squirrels.

To reduce the risk of conversation, chairs will be placed in rows facing the same direction. A guest speaker will read the association bylaws aloud from 1:00 to 3:30, ensuring that no one is left wondering what to talk about.

Some residents have asked whether these measures might make the picnic less fun. The committee wishes to reassure everyone that fun has been carefully considered and kept to a level the insurance company finds acceptable.

Attendance is, of course, voluntary. However, residents who do not attend will receive a friendly reminder letter, a second friendly reminder letter, and a visit from the Friendliness Subcommittee.

We look forward to seeing you there. Please note that the picnic grounds open at 1:00, and that the sign-in table, which is located inside the picnic grounds, closes promptly at noon.$q$, 'draft')
