   $q$The committee calls last year's picnic "a near disaster." What does the author want the reader to conclude from the events listed after that phrase?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The events were harmless, so the committee's alarm is ridiculous.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The events were rare, so the picnic will probably be the same this year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-irony"},{"text":"The events were invented, so the committee cannot be trusted at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The events were dangerous, so the committee was right to act quickly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"takes-speaker-literally"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The events were harmless, so the committee's alarm is ridiculous.$q$, $q$A disk in the potato salad and guests having fun without a form are trivial, so calling them a disaster exposes the committee's absurd sense of proportion. Nothing in the text suggests the events were made up.$q$, 'draft', 'f3dc3dc6-dbf4-557d-9b30-44a4cc4d1e85')
