  ('0441929a-d974-59e3-99a9-6733fb576d86', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The committee says fun "has been carefully considered and kept to a level the insurance company finds acceptable." How does what this sentence says differ from what it reveals?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It claims to answer residents, but it actually changes the subject to the weather.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It claims to quote the insurer, but it actually shows the committee wrote the rules.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It claims fun was reduced, but it actually promises that the picnic will be exciting.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-irony"},{"text":"It claims to reassure residents, but it actually confirms that fun has been reduced.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It claims to reassure residents, but it actually confirms that fun has been reduced.$q$, $q$The sentence is framed as reassurance, yet "kept to a level" admits that fun has been limited, which is exactly what residents feared. It does not promise excitement; it quietly confirms the opposite.$q$, 'draft', 'f3dc3dc6-dbf4-557d-9b30-44a4cc4d1e85')
