   $q$What is the effect of placing "Attendance is, of course, voluntary" directly before the list of reminder letters and the visit from a subcommittee?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The details that follow change the topic, showing that the committee has finished discussing the picnic.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"The details that follow support the claim, showing that the committee respects every resident's choice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"takes-speaker-literally"},{"text":"The details that follow contradict the claim, showing that residents are really being pressured to attend.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The details that follow explain the claim, showing that the letters are only invitations to future events.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-irony"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The details that follow contradict the claim, showing that residents are really being pressured to attend.$q$, $q$Two reminder letters and a home visit are a form of pressure, so the sentences after "voluntary" undercut it. Reading the letters as respectful invitations takes the committee's polite wording at face value.$q$, 'draft', 'f3dc3dc6-dbf4-557d-9b30-44a4cc4d1e85')
