   $q$How does the final sentence about the sign-in table contribute to the meaning of the whole announcement?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It ends on a rule that makes attending impossible, revealing that the rules now serve themselves rather than the residents.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It ends on a friendly invitation, softening the earlier rules so residents feel welcome to come and enjoy themselves.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"takes-speaker-literally"},{"text":"It ends on a practical reminder, showing that the committee has finally become organized and helpful to residents.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-irony"},{"text":"It ends on a scheduling error, suggesting the committee will cancel the picnic once the mistake is discovered.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It ends on a rule that makes attending impossible, revealing that the rules now serve themselves rather than the residents.$q$, $q$No one can sign in at a table inside grounds that open an hour after it closes, so the last rule shuts everyone out and caps the satire of rules that exist for their own sake. Nothing hints that the committee will notice the problem or cancel the event.$q$, 'draft', 'f3dc3dc6-dbf4-557d-9b30-44a4cc4d1e85')
