   $q$When the speaker says the yardstick "will fit in my car, which it will not," what is the speaker doing?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Refusing to take the yardstick because it would not be useful anymore","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Making an honest mistake about the size of the car and the yardstick","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-irony"},{"text":"Telling the grandmother a kind untruth while admitting the truth to the reader","is_correct":true},{"text":"Teasing the grandmother so that she will laugh during a hard afternoon","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Telling the grandmother a kind untruth while admitting the truth to the reader$q$, $q$The speaker says one thing to the grandmother and immediately tells the reader the opposite, so the gap is deliberate and protective. The speaker wraps the yardstick to keep it, so refusing it is wrong.$q$, 'draft', '95df3669-5f25-508b-a6d9-48db3e8976cb')
