   $q$The grandmother calls the new apartment "very sensible," and the next lines mention a parking lot view and a closet with room for one box. What is the effect?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The details shift the setting, showing the rest of the poem takes place inside the new apartment.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"The details undercut the mild word, showing the move as a loss she describes with understatement.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The details contradict the speaker, showing the speaker has never visited the new apartment at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The details support the word, showing the apartment is a practical improvement she is excited about.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"takes-speaker-literally"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The details undercut the mild word, showing the move as a loss she describes with understatement.$q$, $q$A parking lot window and a single box of space after a room full of tins and spools reveal how much is being given up, so "sensible" understates the loss. The poem stays in the old room and on the stairs, so the setting never moves to the apartment.$q$, 'draft', '95df3669-5f25-508b-a6d9-48db3e8976cb')
