  ('2c9492fa-1032-504a-b69d-35f913b787e5', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The narrator says eleven seconds in rowing is "roughly the length of a lunch break." What does this joke suggest about the narrator's attitude?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The narrator is angry that the officials timed the race unfairly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The narrator believes eleven seconds is a very small margin to lose by.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-irony"},{"text":"The narrator can laugh about the loss and does not feel crushed by it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The narrator is mainly interested in what the team ate after racing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The narrator can laugh about the loss and does not feel crushed by it.$q$, $q$The exaggeration pokes fun at how far behind they were, which shows the narrator has made peace with the result. The joke works because eleven seconds is a large gap in rowing, not a small one.$q$, 'draft', '9617c6e6-cebe-592a-a2d3-06d729b873aa')
