  ('2081c64a-0b33-584c-8d53-610988ee3033', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'medium',
   $q$How does revealing the result at the beginning change what the reader pays attention to?$q$, $q$[{"text":"With the outcome settled, the reader focuses on the other schools and the crowds cheering from shore.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"With the outcome settled, the reader focuses on how the team grows rather than on whether it wins.","is_correct":true},{"text":"With the outcome hidden, the reader stays in suspense about the winner until the final paragraph.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-structure"},{"text":"With the outcome settled, the reader loses interest and the story becomes a list of practice drills.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$With the outcome settled, the reader focuses on how the team grows rather than on whether it wins.$q$, $q$Because the loss is announced first, the suspense shifts from "Will they win?" to "What did the season mean?", which the moment at five hundred meters answers. The result is not hidden; it is the first thing the reader learns.$q$, 'draft', '9617c6e6-cebe-592a-a2d3-06d729b873aa')
