-- Passage rg11-literary-structure-pov-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('1f423d1b-86a2-5d31-bb69-326e28f42f48', 'rg11-literary-structure-pov-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '9-12', $q$The Heron and the Ledger$q$, $q$On a wide brown river there lived a heron who believed that most birds fished foolishly. They simply stood in the shallows and struck at whatever swam past. "There is no plan in it," the heron said. "A wise bird would first learn everything about the fish, and then catch only the best ones."

So the heron found a smooth piece of bark and began a ledger. Each morning it recorded every fish that passed its legs: the silver ones, the speckled ones, the ones with a red mark near the tail. It noted their sizes, their speeds, and the hours at which they preferred to travel. The ledger grew thick. The heron grew thin.

A kingfisher who lived on a branch above the bend watched all this with interest. Every day the kingfisher dropped into the water, caught a small fish, and ate it. "Your method is crude," the heron told it. "You have no idea whether that was the best fish." The kingfisher agreed that it had no idea, and went on eating.

By the end of summer, the heron's ledger described every fish in that stretch of river. It knew which ones were fattest, which were slowest, and which came closest to the bank. It was ready, at last, to begin.

That night the first frost came. In the morning, a skin of ice covered the shallows, and the fish had gone down to the deep water where no heron could follow. The other birds were already leaving for the south.

The heron tucked its ledger under one wing and flew after them, late and alone. And so it became the most knowledgeable bird on the river, which is a great comfort, they say, on a long flight with an empty stomach.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
where public.passages.status = 'draft';
