   $q$What does the reader understand that the narrator refuses to admit?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The narrator played the whole sonata without a single mistake.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"takes-speaker-literally"},{"text":"The narrator's mother was disappointed by the performance.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The narrator's brother was the one who felt nervous that day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-character"},{"text":"The narrator was very nervous before and during the recital.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The narrator was very nervous before and during the recital.$q$, $q$Checking music eleven times, shaking hands, and twenty minutes of practice bows all point to nerves the narrator keeps denying. The narrator admits a skipped measure, so the performance was not flawless.$q$, 'draft', '7ab98993-2aaa-5cad-9fd7-88d6ee505a25')
