   $q$Why does the author have the narrator insist again and again on being calm?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The repeated denials become evidence of the very nervousness the narrator is denying.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The repeated denials show that the narrator is trying to calm down a frightened brother.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-character"},{"text":"The repeated denials prove that the narrator has trained to stay relaxed onstage.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"takes-speaker-literally"},{"text":"The repeated denials reveal that the narrator dislikes playing the piano for audiences.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The repeated denials become evidence of the very nervousness the narrator is denying.$q$, $q$A truly calm person would not need to explain it three times, which is why Mateo asks "why I kept explaining it." The narrator is not calming Mateo; Mateo is the one asking questions.$q$, 'draft', '7ab98993-2aaa-5cad-9fd7-88d6ee505a25')
