   $q$Which detail most directly undercuts the narrator's explanation for shaking hands?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The narrator's mother handed over a bottle of water afterward.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-target-evidence"},{"text":"The narrator walked onto the stage slightly faster than reasonable.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-target-evidence"},{"text":"It was June, and the air conditioning had been broken for a week.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The narrator checked the sheet music eleven times in the car.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-target-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It was June, and the air conditioning had been broken for a week.$q$, $q$The narrator blames the cold, but a June building with broken air conditioning would be warm, so this detail directly contradicts the excuse. The eleven checks of the sheet music and the fast walk onstage show nerves too, but they do not answer the claim about the cold.$q$, 'draft', '7ab98993-2aaa-5cad-9fd7-88d6ee505a25')
