   $q$Telling this story through this particular first-person narrator creates humor mainly because:$q$, $q$[{"text":"the narrator switches between several characters' thoughts throughout the story.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-point-of-view"},{"text":"the narrator's confident account keeps clashing with the evidence the narrator reports.","is_correct":true},{"text":"the narrator knows less about the recital than the brother who is telling the story.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-narrator"},{"text":"the narrator describes other musicians making far worse mistakes during the recital.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$the narrator's confident account keeps clashing with the evidence the narrator reports.$q$, $q$The narrator supplies details (eleven checks, a skipped measure) that contradict the claims of calm, and that gap is the joke. The story stays inside one narrator's head and never shows other performers.$q$, 'draft', '7ab98993-2aaa-5cad-9fd7-88d6ee505a25')
