insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('ba6346df-0ea0-5d96-88cf-18925cb69cdd', 'rg11-literary-structure-pov-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Ode to the Group Project$q$, $q$Hear now, all students, the tale of the Group Project,
assigned on a Tuesday, due in two weeks, worth thirty percent.
Four heroes gathered at the long library table:
Desmond the Planner, Ines the Silent, Kofi of the Many Snacks,
and Priya, who would, in the end, do everything.

On the first day they made a shared document.
They named it, and they admired the name.
On the fourth day Desmond made a schedule in seven colors,
a schedule so beautiful that no one dared to follow it.

On the ninth day Kofi brought pretzels, and they were good.
Ines sent a message that said only, "on it,"
and was not heard from again until the presentation,
where she nodded at the slides with great authority.

On the thirteenth night, by the glow of one laptop,
Priya wrote the report, built the slides, and checked the sources,
while across the city her teammates slept
the deep and peaceful sleep of the deserving.

Then came the grading, and behold, the grade was an A,
and it was shared equally among the four,
as the syllabus had promised, and as the heavens intended.
Sing this tale wherever a project is assigned.
Sing it, and then ask who is doing the work.$q$, 'draft')
