  ('0d44c0db-ce21-591f-8747-15d1656ea876', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'medium',
   $q$How does revealing in the first stanza that Priya "would, in the end, do everything" shape the rest of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The reader already knows the outcome, so each teammate's useless effort reads as a knowing joke.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The reader is kept in suspense, so the final stanza surprises everyone with Priya's hard work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-structure"},{"text":"The reader learns Priya's motive, so the poem turns into a study of why she enjoys schoolwork.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The reader doubts the claim, so the later stanzas are needed to prove Priya did nothing at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The reader already knows the outcome, so each teammate's useless effort reads as a knowing joke.$q$, $q$Because the ending is announced early, the reader watches the admired file name, the pretzels and the "on it" message with full awareness of where they lead. The surprise is given away on purpose, so there is no suspense to break.$q$, 'draft', 'ba6346df-0ea0-5d96-88cf-18925cb69cdd')
