  ('620d3056-51c9-5b7d-802e-f696d15bbda6', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The newspaper calls the event "the warmest welcome any piece of machinery had ever received." What attitude toward the town does this line convey?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Harsh criticism of the town for wasting food on a meaningless parade","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"Affectionate amusement that treats a silly mistake with a straight face","is_correct":true},{"text":"Open embarrassment that the newspaper had to report such a story","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"Sincere admiration for the band saw as the most important arrival","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"takes-speaker-literally"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Affectionate amusement that treats a silly mistake with a straight face$q$, $q$Reporting a parade for a crate as a "warm welcome" is deadpan understatement that laughs gently with the town. The story's tone is fond throughout, with no scolding about pies or parades.$q$, 'draft', 'e6cfc567-cd22-59c1-bc46-50a863751977')
