   $q$What is the effect of opening and closing the story with the same lesson, "a violin is mostly air"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The repeated words signal that the story's events happened in reverse chronological order.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"The repeated words suggest the narrator never understood the lesson in all those years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The repeated words frame the story and show their meaning deepening as the narrator grows.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The repeated words show that Mr. Halvorsen had only one lesson and taught nothing else.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The repeated words frame the story and show their meaning deepening as the narrator grows.$q$, $q$The narrator says "It was the same sentence. I was the one who had changed," so the frame measures the narrator's growth in understanding. The first violin's sound shows the narrator did come to understand it.$q$, 'draft', '53059e2f-498a-5425-8a0c-589494b02356')
