  ('1ea42bea-c108-5d2a-b781-ca9e82692c6f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'medium',
   $q$How does the narrator's view of the sentence "a violin is mostly air" differ at the beginning and at the end?$q$, $q$[{"text":"At first the narrator finds it funny; by the end the narrator finds it confusing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-shift"},{"text":"At first it comes from the narrator's mother; by the end it comes from Mr. Halvorsen instead.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-speaker-character"},{"text":"At first the narrator dismisses it as a pose; by the end the narrator receives it as the heart of the craft.","is_correct":true},{"text":"At first the narrator accepts it fully; by the end the narrator rejects it as outdated advice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-structure"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$At first the narrator dismisses it as a pose; by the end the narrator receives it as the heart of the craft.$q$, $q$At fifteen the narrator thought it was something craftsmen "said to sound wise," but after hearing the instrument the narrator knows the sound comes from the enclosed air. Both times the words come from Mr. Halvorsen, not the narrator's mother.$q$, 'draft', '53059e2f-498a-5425-8a0c-589494b02356')
