  ('ccc4299d-2e95-57cf-8adb-b16884407b80', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-main-idea-summary'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Instead of repairing a failing wall, planners at Calder Bay let the tide return. The marsh that grew back builds up sediment against rising seas and draws birds and fish, and despite some costs it now serves as a model.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Calder Bay was farmland for a century until the parks office bought it. The parks office then rebuilt the old wall with concrete so that the fields would stay dry for good.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Wading birds returned to Calder Bay after decades away, and young fish used the new pools as nurseries. Fishing crews soon reported larger catches of several kinds of fish in the bay.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Planners at Calder Bay made a brilliant decision that every other coast should copy. Neighbors who complained about losing their pastures and footpath were being short-sighted about the future.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Instead of repairing a failing wall, planners at Calder Bay let the tide return. The marsh that grew back builds up sediment against rising seas and draws birds and fish, and despite some costs it now serves as a model.$q$, $q$The choice beginning "Instead of repairing a failing wall" covers the decision, both benefits, the costs and the conclusion without judgment. The wildlife choice is accurate but leaves out the shoreline protection and the decision itself.$q$, 'draft', 'cf6ed342-15bb-50cf-9eb3-94e012db2791')
