   $q$What is the effect of the final paragraph's discussion of the project's costs?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that the planners ignored local residents, which is the main lesson other regions should learn.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It undercuts the rest of the passage by suggesting that the project's costs were greater than its benefits.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"It shifts the central idea from coastal protection to the importance of keeping footpaths open to the public.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-emphasis"},{"text":"It acknowledges real drawbacks, which makes the closing claim measured: restoration works well \"in the right places,\" not everywhere.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It acknowledges real drawbacks, which makes the closing claim measured: restoration works well "in the right places," not everywhere.$q$, $q$After naming the costs, the paragraph turns with "Still" and limits its conclusion to "the right places," so the costs make the claim more careful rather than overturning it. Nothing suggests the costs outweighed the benefits.$q$, 'draft', 'cf6ed342-15bb-50cf-9eb3-94e012db2791')
