   $q$Which statement best expresses the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Rowing is the most difficult team sport, because a single mistake by any rower can tip the boat over.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The rower who sits nearest the stern of the boat is called the stroke and sets the rhythm for the crew.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"In rowing, and in many group efforts, how well members work in rhythm can matter more than raw strength.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Strength does not matter at all in rowing, so coaches should choose crews only by timing and rhythm.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$In rowing, and in many group efforts, how well members work in rhythm can matter more than raw strength.$q$, $q$The passage explains why timing matters, how crews train for it, a test at Linwood and a broader lesson. The text says "Strength matters," so the claim that it does not matter at all goes too far.$q$, 'draft', 'fe8e373c-6b7b-5d50-b66f-a797b8a135e6')
