   $q$Which statement best expresses the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Road salt is the greatest danger to bridges, because it causes steel to rust and concrete to weaken.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-emphasis"},{"text":"Expansion joints are a poor design choice, and engineers have stopped using them on every kind of bridge.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Because bridge materials expand and shrink with temperature, engineers design bridges to allow that movement rather than resist it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Drivers can feel a soft thump every few hundred feet as their tires roll over metal strips on long bridges.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because bridge materials expand and shrink with temperature, engineers design bridges to allow that movement rather than resist it.$q$, $q$The final paragraph states the idea that ties the passage together: a bridge must accept "the fact that its materials move." Paragraph 4 says only shorter bridges increasingly avoid joints, so the choice saying engineers have stopped using joints on every kind of bridge overstates it.$q$, 'draft', '26452a93-5902-5bad-acae-1157580c1e77')
