   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Bridge joints use interlocking steel teeth that slide past each other like fingers. Larger bridges use rubber seals and steel beams, and bearings let the deck slide on its supports.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Bridges change length as temperatures rise and fall, and this movement is a serious danger to drivers. Anyone crossing a long bridge in winter should worry about cracks and buckling decks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Bridges change length as temperatures rise and fall, so engineers add joints and bearings that let them move. Since joints let in water and wear out, some shorter bridges are built as flexible units without them.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Bridges change length as temperatures rise and fall, which is why every bridge is now built as one flexible unit. Old joints let in water and wear out, so engineers are removing them everywhere.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Bridges change length as temperatures rise and fall, so engineers add joints and bearings that let them move. Since joints let in water and wear out, some shorter bridges are built as flexible units without them.$q$, $q$The choice ending "some shorter bridges are built as flexible units without them" covers the cause, the solution, its drawbacks and the newer approach accurately. The choice ending "engineers are removing them everywhere" sounds similar but claims "every bridge" is now jointless, while paragraph 4 says only shorter bridges increasingly avoid joints.$q$, 'draft', '26452a93-5902-5bad-acae-1157580c1e77')
