   $q$The speaker compares the sister's handoff to passing "a full glass of water." What does this comparison suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She passes the baton quickly and carelessly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"She dislikes running the third leg of the relay.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She is thirsty by the time she finishes her leg.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"She hands it over cautiously, afraid of a mistake.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She hands it over cautiously, afraid of a mistake.$q$, $q$A full glass must be passed slowly and carefully, and the next line confirms she is "careful, a little late." Reading the comparison as being about thirst takes the image literally.$q$, 'draft', 'a952bb97-3d84-5d6b-b622-89a2478549ae')
