   $q$According to the passage, how did Pruitt usually record that a family had paid its account?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He marked every account paid on the last day of the year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"He crossed out the total and wrote the new balance.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"He tore off a delivery receipt and pressed it in the book.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-details"},{"text":"He wrote \"Pd.\" with the customer's initials and the date.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He wrote "Pd." with the customer's initials and the date.$q$, $q$The second paragraph states the normal pattern: "Pd." beside the total with initials and a date. Marking everything on December 31 is what makes the Castellano account unusual, not the usual practice.$q$, 'draft', 'ec3b98c9-71ed-544e-9759-eba25dd6a1df')
