   $q$Which detail best suggests that 1934 was a difficult year for the Castellano family?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They bought on credit for months, including cough syrup, and paid nothing.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Their entries were all marked paid in darker ink on one date.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-evidence"},{"text":"The ledger was found in a box of old hat forms decades later.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Pruitt's handwriting on their account is cramped and hard to read.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They bought on credit for months, including cough syrup, and paid nothing.$q$, $q$Months of credit purchases during "the dust summer" with no payment point to hardship. The darker ink shows how the debt was later cleared, not what the year was like for the family.$q$, 'draft', 'ec3b98c9-71ed-544e-9759-eba25dd6a1df')
