   $q$What does Felix's decision to hand Amara the pliers and data sheet most strongly suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He wants Amara to replace the old band with a new one.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"He is marking the moment by passing on responsibility to Amara.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He doubts the band number and wants a second opinion.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"He is too excited to hold the pliers steady himself.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"surface-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He is marking the moment by passing on responsibility to Amara.$q$, $q$He tells her to record everything "The way she would," linking Amara to the line of people trained at the station, and the narrator stresses he had never done this before. He already read and checked the number, and he says she does not need to put on a band.$q$, 'draft', 'fd3f5dd4-461b-5acd-94af-e352d8c76197')
