   $q$Which detail best shows that Brisk has changed her opinion of the fox by the end?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She plans to tell every animal at the river.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-moment"},{"text":"She returns and pays an acorn without shouting.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She laughs after reading the sign on the booth.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"She shouts her own name as loudly as she can.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-moment"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She returns and pays an acorn without shouting.$q$, $q$Paying while choosing not to use the echo shows she now values something else the fox provides. Her plan to tell the other animals comes before her walk back up the trail, when she still thought he was a fraud.$q$, 'draft', '6ca79473-7f0b-539b-8f69-1fa6e082c138')
