   $q$How is the passage mainly organized?$q$, $q$[{"text":"By listing reasons that people prefer railway time to local time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-structure"},{"text":"As an argument that towns should return to setting clocks by the sun.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"By comparing the clocks of Ardmoor and Pell Crossing feature by feature.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Chronologically, tracing how timekeeping changed from sun time to railway time.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Chronologically, tracing how timekeeping changed from sun time to railway time.$q$, $q$The passage moves from "two hundred years ago" through the opening of the railway to "within a generation," following the change in order. The two towns are mentioned, but the passage is not a feature-by-feature comparison.$q$, 'draft', 'e6c0f0f7-b15b-56bb-bf59-97e89cf9457a')
