   $q$Which statement best expresses a central theme of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Hiking in the mountains each summer builds strength and patience.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"},{"text":"Glaciers can be saved if scientists measure them often enough.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Family traditions are usually boring until a person grows older.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Carefully witnessing a loss has meaning even when the loss cannot be stopped.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Carefully witnessing a loss has meaning even when the loss cannot be stopped.$q$, $q$The speaker concludes that a record is "a way of paying attention" to "something that is going," even though the aunt "could not stop" the melting. The poem never claims the measurements can save the glacier.$q$, 'draft', '5014dedd-4788-5a9b-815f-3c11a732119c')
