-- Passage rg11-theme-summary-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('d3f6bc26-2ac5-5558-9e14-0c71661a3691', 'rg11-theme-summary-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-theme-summary'), null,
        '9-12', $q$The Margin of the Ledger$q$, $q$The county historical society had received forty boxes from the old Bellweather Mill when the building was sold, and Dae-jung Park had volunteered to help scan them over the summer. Ms. Oyelaran, the archivist, gave him a list on his first morning: owners' letters, contracts, the deed, photographs of the opening ceremony. "We have funding for about two thousand pages," she said. "We start with what researchers ask for."

For three weeks Dae-jung laid letters on the glass and pressed the button. The owners wrote about cotton prices, a new boiler, and a dispute over a railroad siding. The letters were formal and useful, and he forgot each one as soon as the next appeared on the screen.

In the fourth week, he opened a box labeled only "Payroll, 1911 to 1914." Inside were ledgers, column after column of names, hours, and wages. But in the narrow margin of one ledger, someone had written in pencil beside the entries for the weaving floor. Rain again, roof leaks over loom 6. Ada sang the river song at noon and everyone joined. New girl from the farm, fast hands, scared of the noise. The notes were signed with two initials, E.M., and they continued for almost three years.

Dae-jung read them all before lunch. Then he brought the ledger to Ms. Oyelaran's desk and set it open in front of her.

"It isn't on the list," he said. "But nobody else in these boxes tells you what it was like to work there."

She read for a long time. "If we scan this, something else waits another year," she said. "Maybe longer."

"I know."

The next day she rewrote the list in her own handwriting and moved the payroll ledgers near the top. When Dae-jung entered the first scanned page into the online catalog, he came to the field marked Creator. Every record before it said Bellweather Mill Company. He looked at the margin notes again, and then he typed: E.M., weaver, identity unknown.$q$, 'draft')
