   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A father finds a broken bolt on a bridge and has the bridge closed for repairs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"},{"text":"A speaker describes the sky turning the color of weak tea at dawn.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"A speaker feels sorry for a father whose job is boring and unimportant.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"A speaker joins a father on a night bridge inspection, comes to value work no one sees, and now listens to bridges the same way.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A speaker joins a father on a night bridge inspection, comes to value work no one sees, and now listens to bridges the same way.$q$, $q$The correct choice traces the inspection, the speaker's new understanding, and the final habit. The poem never says the bridge was closed, and calling the job unimportant contradicts the speaker's conclusion.$q$, 'draft', '391883cd-e59b-59f4-96ca-3600b90501f6')
