   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the fable?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A proud old mapmaker gets exactly what he deserves when a clever young rival takes all his customers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"A child asks a mapmaker for directions to her grandmother's farm and tells him a bridge washed away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"A mapmaker and his former apprentice form a business together after a flood changes the valley.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"},{"text":"After a flood moves the river, a famous mapmaker insists his maps are right, loses customers to a former apprentice, and finally remeasures and updates his work.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$After a flood moves the river, a famous mapmaker insists his maps are right, loses customers to a former apprentice, and finally remeasures and updates his work.$q$, $q$The correct choice covers the flood, Orrin's refusal, his loss of business, and his change. The choice saying Orrin "gets exactly what he deserves" judges him, and the fable never says he and Liesl join businesses.$q$, 'draft', 'bab7329c-41a8-5098-83e6-e160f484dcd1')
