   $q$The Latin root loqu means "speak," and the suffix -acious means "full of" or "inclined to." What does "loquacious" tell you about Priya?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She tends to argue in a hostile way","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"She tends to write very long notes","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"She tends to talk a great deal","is_correct":true},{"text":"She tends to speak only when asked","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She tends to talk a great deal$q$, $q$Loqu plus -acious means "inclined to speak," which fits the detail that she "could talk for ten minutes about almost anything." Speaking only when asked describes Tobias, not Priya.$q$, 'draft', 'a2ed043a-a576-5361-a12b-59833aa13adb')
