  ('b3918766-8431-5512-99b4-ce8c88795be5', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The prefix ad- means "to" or "toward," and the root voc means "call" or "voice." What were Priya and Tobias assigned to do when they had to "advocate" for the change?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Speak publicly in support of keeping the library open later","is_correct":true},{"text":"Vote on whether the library should stay open later","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"Call the library to ask about its current hours","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"Argue that the library should close earlier instead","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Speak publicly in support of keeping the library open later$q$, $q$To advocate is to lend your voice toward a cause, and the pair "gathered evidence" to support the later hours. Calling the library takes the root "call" too literally and ignores the debate context.$q$, 'draft', 'a2ed043a-a576-5361-a12b-59833aa13adb')
