   $q$The root vers means "turn," and the suffix -ity forms a noun meaning "the quality of." What does "versatility" mean in the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The quality of being stronger than one's opponents","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"The quality of being able to adapt to many different uses","is_correct":true},{"text":"The quality of being able to repeat one motion perfectly","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"The quality of being able to spin quickly in place","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The quality of being able to adapt to many different uses$q$, $q$Versatility is the ability to turn easily to different tasks, like using a weaker foot or hand when needed. Spinning in place takes the root "turn" too literally and does not match the examples in the paragraph.$q$, 'draft', 'dc3eaa1d-85e2-5b3d-979e-c317babdffc8')
