   $q$The suffix -ence turns the adjective "virulent" into a noun. What does the "virulence" of the fungus refer to?$q$, $q$[{"text":"How easily scientists could see it","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"How weak it became over the decades","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"How severely and quickly it caused harm","is_correct":true},{"text":"How long it had existed in nature","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$How severely and quickly it caused harm$q$, $q$Virulent means severe or harmful, so virulence names that quality, shown by the fungus "spreading quickly and overwhelming trees." The weaker strains appear later in the passage, so calling virulence weakness reverses the meaning.$q$, 'draft', '995df5ae-8188-5b3e-9d61-2a6ea1f2e03c')
