   $q$The root path appears in "pathologists," "pathogen," and "apathy," but it can mean "disease" or "feeling," and the prefix a- means "without." What does "apathy" mean in the final paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A careful habit of reporting symptoms","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"A strong fear of becoming infected","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"A complete freedom from any disease","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-sense-of-root"},{"text":"A lack of interest or concern about a problem","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A lack of interest or concern about a problem$q$, $q$Here path means "feeling," so apathy is being without feeling or concern, as when people assume "the problem belongs to someone else." Reading path as "disease" gives "freedom from disease," which does not fit the sentence about public attitudes.$q$, 'draft', '995df5ae-8188-5b3e-9d61-2a6ea1f2e03c')
