   $q$The Greek prefix poly- means "many," and glot means "tongue" or "language." What is a "polyglot"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A person who plays many different games","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-second-root"},{"text":"A person who knows several languages","is_correct":true},{"text":"A person who has lived in many countries","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"A person who talks much more than others","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A person who knows several languages$q$, $q$Poly plus glot means "many tongues," and Kofi is "comfortable in English, French, and Twi." Talking a lot would be loquacious, which is about quantity of speech, not number of languages.$q$, 'draft', '5a92fa28-9abe-56ef-82f3-14efcea084e7')
