  ('a57b2738-d3c3-5251-9655-bb61ad13b7fc', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The Latin root vers means "turn." Why did the interpreter job require Kofi to be "more versatile" than he expected?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It required him to translate the rules over and over.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"It required him to rotate between chess boards every hour.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"It required him to turn to many different kinds of tasks.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It required him to play chess against visiting players.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It required him to turn to many different kinds of tasks.$q$, $q$Versatile describes someone who turns easily to many uses, and Kofi translated rules, found a bus, and explained a seating chart in one morning. Rotating between boards treats "turn" too literally as physical movement.$q$, 'draft', '5a92fa28-9abe-56ef-82f3-14efcea084e7')
